rews, a first-time statewide candidate who has dramatically outraised the incumbent and drawn millions in outside spending against Graham. Recent polls show an unexpectedly close contest, with Graham leading by only one to five points in most surveys, and the lone October debate drew heavy national attention amid Republican nervousness.\n\nStill, the state's strong Republican lean, a unanimous set of expert ratings placing the race at Lean or Likely Republican, and prediction markets pricing Graham around 80-85% all temper the polling optimism for Andrews. The forecast expects Graham to win by roughly four points, with meaningful uncertainty given the thin and sponsor-skewed polling and Andrews' financial capacity to close the gap late.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1565, "margin": -5.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2122, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2115, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2143, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1474, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2135, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2708, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2623, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2878, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2627, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2896, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2599, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2566, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.194, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1953, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2084, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1997, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2291, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.2418, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.192, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.2923, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.223, "mar